  "objective": "Review the rendered UI as if you did not write it.\n\nDo not defend the current implementation.\n\nCompare the rendered result against the intended product direction and identify visible problems that are actually present in the screenshot/browser, not hypothetical code-quality issues.\n\nPrioritize:\n\n* visual hierarchy,\n* alignment,\n* spacing rhythm,\n* text measure,\n* density,\n* balance,\n* surface hierarchy,\n* icon alignment,\n* interaction affordance,\n* unnecessary visual chrome.\n\nLook specifically for:\n\n* areas that feel cramped;\n* areas that feel artificially empty;\n* repeated card shapes;\n* excessive corner radius;\n* weak distinction between primary and secondary information;\n* assistant content that visually feels like a separate product;\n* controls whose importance is overstated;\n* inconsistent spacing or baselines;\n* accidental visual noise.\n\nMake one additional polish pass.\n\nDo not expand scope or add new features.\n\nPrefer deleting or simplifying styling over adding decoration whenever both solve the same problem. 即时同步仓库与更新部署",
